      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Statutory Interstate e-Way Bills, Regulatory Clearances &amp; 100% Marine Insurance for transporter from nagpur to alwar</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p>Shipping goods from Nagpur to Alwar requires three statutory documents: a GST e‑Way Bill, an IBA‑approved Lorry Receipt (LR) or Bilty, and a full‑value marine transit insurance policy that complies with IRDAI rules.</p>

<p>The GST e‑Way Bill is generated on the GSTN portal before the vehicle leaves Maharashtra. It records the consignor’s GSTIN, consignee details, description of goods, and the total declared value. The e‑Way Bill number must be displayed on the dashboard and presented to transport police or customs officials on demand.</p>

<p>An IBA‑approved Lorry Receipt serves as the legal contract between shipper and carrier. It lists each item’s weight, packaging, loading and unloading points, and the freight charges. Because the format is certified by the Indian Banks’ Association, the LR is admissible in court for claim settlement, which is essential for high‑value consignments.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


